@module level1data ; Level 1
@about The level's body: the header the game reads at $C4AE, the sprites, the object table, the metatiles, the map, the wave script, the enemy kinds and their movement scripts, the two mover tables and the movers.
$C4AE b L1Header ; The level header: restart point, checkpoints and the pointers the game reads
> Restart column $00, restart wave $0000; checkpoint columns $06, $25, $4B with wave entries $E788, $E8AF, $EA44; objects $D7F9, map $E571, kinds $EFFB, movers $F365 and $F385.
$C4AF L1RestartWave ; the wave entry a life restarts at (the game keeps its live copy here)
$C4B1 L1Checks ; three checkpoint columns (CheckRestart)
$C4B4 L1WaveStarts ; the wave entries of the start and the checkpoints
$C4BA L1Pointers ; objects, map, kinds, movers 1, movers 2
$C4C4 b L1Spare ; zeros up to the sprites
$C4E0 b L1Sprites 9 ; The level's sprites: cells of 9 bytes (attribute, 8 pixel bytes) the object table points at
@res levels/level1/sprites.bin
$D7F9 b L1Objects 4 ; The level's object table: width, height, the cells' address (LevelObject)
@res levels/level1/objects.bin
$D911 b L1Metatiles 9 ; The metatiles, 144 bytes each (4 x 4 cells of 9 bytes), numbered down from the map: metatile n at $E571 - 144 x (n + 1) (MetatileAddress); 22 of them
@res levels/level1/metatiles.bin
$E571 b L1Map 5 ; The map: 5 bytes a block column (107 columns), each byte a metatile (bits 0-5) and its drawer (bits 6-7)
@res levels/level1/map.bin
$E788 b L1Waves ; The wave script: entries (scroll position, kind, script) RunWaves starts; then the enemies' movement scripts
